<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>

<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

<title>Motion | PhysicsAI 5054</title>

<style>

/* =========================================================
   GLOBAL
========================================================= */

* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

:root {

    --paper: #f7f8fa;
    --paper-2: #eef1f4;
    --card: #ffffff;

    --ink: #172033;
    --ink-soft: #5d6878;
    --ink-faint: #8993a1;

    --line: #dfe4ea;

    --flare: #E8541F;
    --flare-ink: #b83f18;

    --grav: #137A56;
    --grav-ink: #0d6547;

    --radius: 12px;

    --disp: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    --body: "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif;
    --mono: "Courier New", monospace;
}

html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
}

body {
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--body);
    line-height: 1.65;
}

.wrap {
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px 100px;
}


/* =========================================================
   HERO
========================================================= */

header.hero {
    padding: 64px 24px 40px;
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: relative;
}

.kicker {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--flare-ink);

    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
}

.kicker::before {
    content: '';
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--flare);
    display: inline-block;
}

h1.title {
    font-family: var(--disp);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(48px, 9vw, 88px);
    margin: 8px 0 6px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 0.95;
}

.subtitle {
    font-family: var(--body);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 18px;
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
}

.credit {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
}


/* =========================================================
   TICKER
========================================================= */

.tickertape {
    height: 34px;
    margin: 56px 0;

    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    position: relative;
}

.tickertape .rail {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: 50%;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
}

.tickertape .dots {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
}

.tickertape .dots span {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink);
    flex: none;
}

.tickertape .cap {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);

    position: absolute;
    right: 0;
    top: -18px;

    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .06em;
}


/* =========================================================
   SECTIONS
========================================================= */

section {
    margin: 56px 0;
}

.eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--flare-ink);

    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .08em;

    margin-bottom: 6px;
}

section.grav .eyebrow {
    color: var(--grav-ink);
}

h2 {
    font-family: var(--disp);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 30px;

    margin: 0 0 14px;

    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
}

h3 {
    font-family: var(--disp);
    font-size: 23px;
    margin: 24px 0 10px;
}

p {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    color: var(--ink);
}

p.lead {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
}


/* =========================================================
   FORMULA
========================================================= */

.formula {
    font-family: var(--mono);

    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);

    border-left: 4px solid var(--flare);

    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;

    padding: 18px 20px;

    margin: 20px 0;

    font-size: 17px;
}

section.grav .formula {
    border-left-color: var(--grav);
}

.formula .name {
    display: block;

    font-size: 11px;

    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .06em;

    color: var(--ink-faint);

    margin-bottom: 6px;
}


/* =========================================================
   TABLES
========================================================= */

table.symbols,
.uniform-table {

    width: 100%;

    border-collapse: collapse;

    margin: 16px 0;

    font-family: var(--mono);

    font-size: 14px;
}

table.symbols th,
table.symbols td,
.uniform-table th,
.uniform-table td {

    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);

    padding: 9px 10px;

    text-align: left;
}

table.symbols th,
.uniform-table th {

    color: var(--ink-faint);

    font-weight: 500;

    text-transform: uppercase;

    font-size: 11px;

    letter-spacing: .05em;
}

.uniform-table th,
.uniform-table td {
    text-align: center;
}


/* =========================================================
   QUESTION CARDS
========================================================= */

.qcard {

    background: var(--card);

    border: 1px solid var(--line);

    border-radius: var(--radius);

    padding: 20px 22px;

    margin: 18px 0;
}

.qcard .qlabel {

    font-family: var(--mono);

    font-size: 12px;

    color: var(--flare-ink);

    font-weight: 700;

    margin-bottom: 6px;
}

.qcard .qtext {

    font-size: 16px;

    margin-bottom: 14px;
}

.qrow {

    display: flex;

    flex-wrap: wrap;

    gap: 10px;

    align-items: center;
}

.qrow input {

    font-family: var(--mono);

    font-size: 15px;

    padding: 8px 10px;

    border: 1px solid var(--line);

    border-radius: 6px;

    background: var(--paper);

    color: var(--ink);

    width: 140px;
}

.qrow input[type="text"] {
    width: 180px;
}

.qrow span.u {

    font-family: var(--mono);

    font-size: 13px;

    color: var(--ink-faint);
}

button.check {

    font-family: var(--mono);

    font-size: 13px;

    font-weight: 700;

    letter-spacing: .03em;

    background: var(--ink);

    color: #fff;

    border: none;

    border-radius: 6px;

    padding: 9px 16px;

    cursor: pointer;
}

button.check:hover {
    background: var(--flare-ink);
}

.feedback {

    margin-top: 12px;

    font-size: 14px;

    font-family: var(--mono);

    padding: 10px 12px;

    border-radius: 6px;

    display: none;
}

.feedback.show {
    display: block;
}

.feedback.correct {

    background: #E4F3EC;

    color: var(--grav-ink);
}

.feedback.wrong {

    background: #FCE9E4;

    color: var(--flare-ink);
}


/* =========================================================
   GRAPH
========================================================= */

.graphwrap {

    background: var(--card);

    border: 1px solid var(--line);

    border-radius: var(--radius);

    padding: 20px;

    margin: 20px 0;
}

svg text {
    font-family: var(--mono);
}

.axis-label {

    font-size: 11px;

    fill: var(--ink-faint);
}

.gridline {

    stroke: var(--paper-2);

    stroke-width: 1;
}

.axisline {

    stroke: var(--ink-soft);

    stroke-width: 1.4;
}


/* =========================================================
   INTERACTIVE GRAPH BUTTONS
========================================================= */

.shape-gallery {

    display: flex;

    gap: 10px;

    flex-wrap: wrap;

    margin: 14px 0;
}

.shape-btn {

    font-family: var(--mono);

    font-size: 12px;

    padding: 8px 14px;

    border-radius: 20px;

    border: 1px solid var(--line);

    background: var(--card);

    cursor: pointer;

    color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.shape-btn.active {

    background: var(--flare);

    border-color: var(--flare);

    color: #fff;
}

.shape-desc {

    font-size: 15px;

    color: var(--ink-soft);

    margin-top: 6px;

    min-height: 44px;
}


/* =========================================================
   REVEAL
========================================================= */

.toggle-btn {

    font-family: var(--mono);

    font-size: 13px;

    background: transparent;

    border: 1px solid var(--line);

    border-radius: 6px;

    padding: 8px 14px;

    cursor: pointer;

    color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.toggle-btn:hover {

    border-color: var(--ink-soft);

    color: var(--ink);
}

.reveal {

    margin-top: 14px;

    padding: 14px 16px;

    background: var(--paper-2);

    border-radius: 8px;

    font-family: var(--mono);

    font-size: 13.5px;

    display: none;

    line-height: 1.9;
}

.reveal.show {
    display: block;
}

.reveal b {
    color: var(--ink);
}


/* =========================================================
   GRAVITY EXPERIMENT
========================================================= */

.tube-demo {

    display: flex;

    gap: 28px;

    flex-wrap: wrap;

    align-items: flex-start;
}

.tube {

    width: 64px;

    height: 220px;

    border: 2px solid var(--ink-soft);

    border-radius: 8px;

    position: relative;

    background: var(--card);

    flex: none;
}

.tube .coin,
.tube .feather {

    position: absolute;

    left: 50%;

    transform: translateX(-50%);

    top: 12px;

    transition: top 1.5s linear;
}

.tube .coin {

    width: 16px;

    height: 16px;

    border-radius: 50%;

    background: var(--flare);
}

.tube .feather {

    width: 20px;

    height: 10px;

    border-radius: 0 50% 50% 0;

    background: var(--grav);

    top: 12px;
}

.tube-controls {

    display: flex;

    flex-direction: column;

    gap: 10px;
}

.tube-note {

    font-size: 14px;

    color: var(--ink-soft);

    max-width: 40ch;
}


/* =========================================================
   FOOTER
========================================================= */

footer {

    max-width: 880px;

    margin: 0 auto;

    padding: 40px 24px 80px;

    font-family: var(--mono);

    font-size: 11px;

    color: var(--ink-faint);

    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
}


/* =========================================================
   MOBILE
========================================================= */

@media(max-width:600px) {

    header.hero {

        padding: 44px 18px 24px;
    }

    .wrap {

        padding: 0 18px 100px;
    }

    .qrow {

        align-items: stretch;

    }

    .qrow input {

        width: 100%;

    }

}

</style>

</head>


<body>


<!-- =====================================================
     HERO
===================================================== -->

<header class="hero">

<div class="kicker">
PhysicsAI 5054 · Cambridge O Level Physics
</div>

<h1 class="title">
Motion
</h1>

<p class="subtitle">

Describing how objects move using distance, speed,
velocity, acceleration and graphs.

</p>

<div class="credit">

Interactive Learning Chapter · PhysicsAI 5054

</div>

</header>


<div class="wrap">


<!-- =====================================================
     LEARNING PATH
===================================================== -->

<div class="tickertape">

<div class="rail"></div>

<div class="dots">

<span></span>
<span></span>
<span></span>
<span></span>
<span></span>
<span></span>

</div>

<div class="cap">
Motion · From movement to graphs
</div>

</div>


<!-- =====================================================
     1. MOTION
===================================================== -->

<section>

<div class="eyebrow">
01 · Describing Motion
</div>

<h2>
What is motion?
</h2>

<p class="lead">

An object is said to be in motion when its position changes
with time relative to a reference point.

</p>

<p>

To describe motion quantitatively, we use physical quantities
such as <b>distance</b>, <b>speed</b>, <b>velocity</b> and
<b>acceleration</b>.

</p>

<table class="symbols">

<tr>
<th>Quantity</th>
<th>Symbol</th>
<th>SI unit</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>distance</td>
<td>s</td>
<td>metre (m)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>speed</td>
<td>v</td>
<td>metre per second (m/s)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>velocity</td>
<td>v</td>
<td>metre per second (m/s)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>acceleration</td>
<td>a</td>
<td>metre per second squared (m/s²)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>time</td>
<td>t</td>
<td>second (s)</td>
</tr>

</table>

</section>


<!-- =====================================================
     2. SPEED
===================================================== -->

<section>

<div class="eyebrow">
02 · Speed
</div>

<h2>
Speed
</h2>

<p>

Speed tells us how quickly an object is moving.

</p>

<div class="formula">

<span class="name">
Definition of speed
</span>

speed = distance travelled ÷ time taken

</div>

<p>

The SI unit of speed is <b>m/s</b>.

</p>


<div class="qcard">

<div class="qlabel">
Qu 1
</div>

<div class="qtext">

Deduce the SI unit of speed.

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="text"
id="q1"
placeholder="e.g. m/s">

<button
class="check"
onclick="checkText('q1','m/s','fb1')">

Check

</button>

</div>

<div
class="feedback"
id="fb1">
</div>

</div>


<div class="qcard">

<div class="qlabel">
Qu 2
</div>

<div class="qtext">

In a 100 m race, the winner's time is 12.0 s.
What is her average speed for this race?

</div>

<div class="formula">

<span class="name">
Reminder
</span>

average speed = total distance ÷ total time taken

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="number"
id="q2"
step="0.01"
placeholder="answer">

<span class="u">
m/s
</span>

<button
class="check"
onclick="checkNumber('q2',8.33,0.05,'fb2')">

Check

</button>

</div>

<div
class="feedback"
id="fb2">
</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =====================================================
     3. VELOCITY
===================================================== -->

<section>

<div class="eyebrow">
03 · Velocity
</div>

<h2>
Velocity
</h2>

<p>

Velocity is the speed of an object in a specified direction.

</p>

<p>

Unlike speed, velocity is a <b>vector quantity</b>.
It therefore has both magnitude and direction.

</p>

<div class="qcard">

<div class="qlabel">
Qu 3
</div>

<div class="qtext">

What is the SI unit of velocity?

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="text"
id="q3"
placeholder="unit">

<button
class="check"
onclick="checkText('q3','m/s','fb3')">

Check

</button>

</div>

<div
class="feedback"
id="fb3">
</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =====================================================
     4. ACCELERATION
===================================================== -->

<section>

<div class="eyebrow">
04 · Acceleration
</div>

<h2>
Acceleration
</h2>

<p>

Acceleration is defined as the <b>rate of change of velocity
with time</b>.

</p>

<div class="formula">

<span class="name">
Acceleration
</span>

a = (v − u) ÷ t

</div>

<table class="symbols">

<tr>
<th>Quantity</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>u</td>
<td>initial velocity</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>v</td>
<td>final velocity</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>t</td>
<td>time taken</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>a</td>
<td>acceleration</td>
</tr>

</table>


<div class="qcard">

<div class="qlabel">
Qu 4
</div>

<div class="qtext">

What is the acceleration of a Mercedes car if it travels
at a constant speed of 200 km/h for half an hour?

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="number"
id="q4"
step="0.01">

<span class="u">
m/s²
</span>

<button
class="check"
onclick="checkNumber('q4',0,0.01,'fb4')">

Check

</button>

</div>

<div
class="feedback"
id="fb4">
</div>

</div>


<div class="qcard">

<div class="qlabel">
Qu 5
</div>

<div class="qtext">

A body accelerates for 25 s and its velocity increases
from 250 m/s to 325 m/s. Calculate its acceleration.

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="number"
id="q5"
step="0.01">

<span class="u">
m/s²
</span>

<button
class="check"
onclick="checkNumber('q5',3,0.05,'fb5')">

Check

</button>

</div>

<div
class="feedback"
id="fb5">
</div>

</div>


<div class="qcard">

<div class="qlabel">
Qu 6
</div>

<div class="qtext">

A body starts from rest and accelerates uniformly at
2.5 m/s² for 15 s. Deduce its final velocity.

</div>

<div class="formula">

<span class="name">
Useful relationship
</span>

v = u + at

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="number"
id="q6"
step="0.1">

<span class="u">
m/s
</span>

<button
class="check"
onclick="checkNumber('q6',37.5,0.1,'fb6')">

Check

</button>

</div>

<div
class="feedback"
id="fb6">
</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =====================================================
     5. UNIFORM ACCELERATION
===================================================== -->

<section>

<div class="eyebrow">
05 · Uniform Acceleration
</div>

<h2>
Uniform acceleration
</h2>

<p>

A body is said to be moving with <b>uniform acceleration</b>
if its velocity increases uniformly or linearly with time.

</p>

<table class="uniform-table">

<tr>

<th>Time / s</th>

<td>0</td>
<td>4</td>
<td>8</td>
<td>12</td>
<td>16</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<th>Velocity / m/s</th>

<td>0</td>
<td>10</td>
<td>20</td>
<td>30</td>
<td>40</td>

</tr>

</table>

<p>

After every 4 seconds, the velocity increases by 10 m/s.

This means that the acceleration is constant.

</p>

<div class="formula">

<span class="name">
Acceleration
</span>

a = change in velocity ÷ time taken

</div>


::contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}


</section>


<!-- =====================================================
     6. DISTANCE-TIME GRAPHS
===================================================== -->

<section>

<div class="eyebrow">
06 · Distance–Time Graphs
</div>

<h2>
Distance–time graphs
</h2>

<p>

A distance–time graph shows how the distance travelled by
an object changes with time.

</p>

<p>

The <b>gradient of a distance–time graph gives the speed</b>
of the object.

</p>

<div class="formula">

<span class="name">
Gradient of distance–time graph
</span>

speed = change in distance ÷ change in time

</div>

<h3>
Example
</h3>

<table class="uniform-table">

<tr>

<th>Time / s</th>

<td>0</td>
<td>10</td>
<td>20</td>
<td>30</td>
<td>40</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<th>Distance / m</th>

<td>0</td>
<td>20</td>
<td>40</td>
<td>60</td>
<td>80</td>

</tr>

</table>

<div class="graphwrap">

<svg
viewBox="0 0 500 300"
width="100%">

<line
class="axisline"
x1="60"
y1="250"
x2="460"
y2="250"/>

<line
class="axisline"
x1="60"
y1="30"
x2="60"
y2="250"/>

<polyline
points="60,250 160,195 260,140 360,85 460,30"
fill="none"
stroke="#E8541F"
stroke-width="4"/>

<text
class="axis-label"
x="260"
y="285"
text-anchor="middle">

time / s

</text>

<text
class="axis-label"
x="18"
y="140"
text-anchor="middle"
transform="rotate(-90 18 140)">

distance / m

</text>

</svg>

</div>


<div class="qcard">

<div class="qlabel">
Qu 7
</div>

<div class="qtext">

Using the graph above:

<br><br>

(a) What is the total distance travelled?<br>
(b) What is the total time of travel?<br>
(c) Calculate the average speed.<br>
(d) Calculate the gradient of the line.<br>
(e) What can you deduce?

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="number"
id="q7a"
placeholder="(a)">

<span class="u">
m
</span>

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="number"
id="q7b"
placeholder="(b)">

<span class="u">
s
</span>

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="number"
id="q7c"
placeholder="(c)">

<span class="u">
m/s
</span>

</div>

<div class="qrow">

<input
type="number"
id="q7d"
placeholder="(d)">

<span class="u">
m/s
</span>

</div>

<br>

<button
class="check"
onclick="checkQ7()">

Check (a)–(d)

</button>

<div
class="feedback"
id="fb7">
</div>

</div>


<h3>
Interpreting distance–time graphs
</h3>

<div class="shape-gallery">

<button
class="shape-btn active"
onclick="showDT('uniform')">

Uniform speed

</button>

<button
class="shape-btn"
onclick="showDT('rest')">

At rest

</button>

<button
class="shape-btn"
onclick="showDT('fast')">

Increasing speed

</button>

<button
class="shape-btn"
onclick="showDT('slow')">

Decreasing speed

</button>

</div>

<div class="graphwrap">

<svg
viewBox="0 0 300 160"
width="100%"
id="dtGraph">

<line
class="axisline"
x1="30"
y1="140"
x2="280"
y2="140"/>

<line
class="axisline"
x1="30"
y1="20"
x2="30"
y2="140"/>

<path
id="dtPath"
d="M30 140 L270 30"
fill="none"
stroke="#E8541F"
stroke-width="4"/>

</svg>

<p
class="shape-desc"
id="dtDesc">

A straight sloping line represents uniform speed.

</p>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =====================================================
     7. VELOCITY-TIME GRAPHS
===================================================== -->

<section>

<div class="eyebrow">
07 · Velocity–Time Graphs
</div>

<h2>
Velocity–time graphs
</h2>

<p>

A velocity–time graph shows how the velocity of a body
changes with time.

</p>

<p>

Two important quantities can be obtained from the graph:

</p>

<div class="formula">

<span class="name">
Gradient
</span>

acceleration = change in velocity ÷ time

</div>

<div class="formula">

<span class="name">
Area
</span>

distance travelled = area under velocity–time graph

</div>

<h3>
