<div class="qcard">

<div class="qlabel">
Qu 10
</div>

<div class="qtext">

Use the graph to determine:

<br><br>

(a) total time of travel<br>
(b) maximum speed reached<br>
(c) final speed<br>
(d) acceleration O→A<br>
(e) deceleration B→C<br>
(f) total distance covered<br>
(g) average speed for the whole journey

</div>

<button
class="toggle-btn"
onclick="toggle('q10')">

Reveal worked answers

</button>

<div
class="reveal"
id="q10">

(a) Total time = <b>40 s</b><br>

(b) Maximum speed = <b>10 m/s</b><br>

(c) Final speed = <b>0 m/s</b><br><br>

(d) Acceleration O→A:

(10 − 0) ÷ 10 = <b>+1 m/s²</b><br><br>

(e) Acceleration B→C:

(0 − 10) ÷ 10 = <b>−1 m/s²</b><br>

The magnitude of the deceleration is therefore
<b>1 m/s²</b>.<br><br>

(f) Total distance = area under graph

= ½(10)(10) + (20)(10) + ½(10)(10)

= 50 + 200 + 50

= <b>300 m</b><br><br>

(g) Average speed

= total distance ÷ total time

= 300 ÷ 40

= <b>7.5 m/s</b>

</div>

</div>

