<h2>
Acceleration due to gravity, g
</h2>

<p>

When an object is allowed to fall freely under the Earth's
gravitational pull, its velocity increases steadily.

It therefore experiences a constant acceleration.

</p>

<p>

This acceleration is called the
<b>acceleration due to gravity</b> and is represented by
<b>g</b>.

</p>

<div class="formula">

<span class="name">
Acceleration due to gravity
</span>

g ≈ 9.81 m/s²

<br><br>

For many O Level calculations:

g ≈ 10 m/s²

</div>


::contentReference[oaicite:1]{index=1}



